WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.830
For a hundred years the Astragius galaxy
had been split by war.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:42.170
I was ordered into an operation
whose details were kept from me.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.380
There, my destiny was changed
the moment I saw her.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.830
She was apparently the military's greatest secret.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.000
Since deserting the army, my wanderings
had brought me to the city of Uoodo.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.290
And while in battle, I met her once more.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:10.080
She's deeply tied to my destiny.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.710
But what sort of destiny is it?

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.630
Bonds

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.000
Where's Chirico?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.460
We're sending in a patrol to see.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.540
We can't find the Prototype, can we?!

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.670
The Prototype couldn't possibly have lost to him!

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.920
I knew she wasn't a fully functional PS!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.170
Now I have to take responsibility for this, Borough!

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.460
She's failed.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.750
I've always seen you.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.540
Always?

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.040
Yes, always.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.670
This is only the third time we've met.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.790
The first was on the Lido research base.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.420
The second was at the jijirium storage site.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.750
And then now.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.880
Were you ordered to kill me?

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:21.130
Chief Iskui and Father Borough
ordered me to do this.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.460
Why didn't you kill me?

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:24.710
You could have.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.630
I don't know.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:29.290
I just... just didn't want to fight you.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.290
Who are you?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.580
I don't know.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.000
I don't even know my own name!

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.880
Proto One. That code name is my name now.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.630
Tell me. What were they doing
at the research station?

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.290
What were they trying to achieve?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.040
I don't know! I don't know anything!

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.880
Move it! If he spots us on the monitor,
we're screwed.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.920
My consciousness began with my birth.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.460
With the first thing I saw.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.790
And that was you.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.210
It was the first light I saw as I was being born.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:20.830
That was when I...

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:24.000
When I attacked Lido while under
Capt. Oriya's command.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.330
It was an allied base.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.460
I didn't know any of the details of the operation.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.250
I was following orders. That's all.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.960
That's what a soldier does.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.920
I also fight because they order me to.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.210
You all right?

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.000
I'm fine! Gotta tell them!

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.380
It's too dangerous to stay here,
now that they know where we are!

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:56.630
Wait!

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.460
I came here to see you.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.750
To ask you what I wanted to know.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.420
I can't die yet.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:05.790
Neither can I.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.830
Chief, we've found Chirico.
He's in Command and Control.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.540
Command and Control?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.330
Of course. From there he can spot
anyone trying to get in.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:22.210
It also looked like the Prototype
was helping him.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.170
What?!

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.380
Son of a...! Launch missiles!
Launch a strike on Command and Control!

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.580
You mean kill the Prototype along with him?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.750
At this point it doesn't matter!

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:32.380
Sir!

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.500
Wait!

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.080
Chief, you can't! We still need her!

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.330
Is there any other way?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.170
Fight ATs with ATs.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.880
We'll send the Battling pilots out after them.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.130
Will they cooperate with us?

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:50.170
They will if we grant the Battling industry in Uoodo
special legal status in return for helping us.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.080
Chirico, what's your radio set to?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.290
20.5 MHz, but it's broken. I can't transmit.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.790
That doesn't matter. I'll be the one transmitting.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.330
Switch it on.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.210
Right.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.500
It's a signal from Chirico. He's still alive!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.750
Gimme that!

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.630
Hello. Hello, Chirico. Do you read? This is Gotho.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.420
Answer me. You still alive, Chirico?

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:22.790
Who's that?

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:24.920
A friend. He's nearby.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.170
We'd better hurry.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.580
The police will be coming soon.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:31.380
Yes, but if we don't hurry...

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:32.880
I understand.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.710
We'd better get going. Stick close to me.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:37.920
What's going on?

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.080
Let's go.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.130
Looks like Chirico's with that woman.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.250
Yeah, and I'd say his radio's been damaged, too.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.880
"That woman?"

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.540
What's goin' on here?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.130
Why'd they call us out?

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.040
Greetings. I'm Chief Iskui.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.920
And I'm quite familiar with what you all do.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.460
Don't screw with me!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.500
Just chill, law man.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.000
You mentioned a special condition, right?

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.290
About giving us special status here in Uoodo.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.460
I guarantee it.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.500
However, you must not kill the girl.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.880
All right, you can count me in.
I've been hearing about this guy.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.420
I'd just like one crack at him.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.920
We're all set. You'd better get going.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.540
Then we'll move out.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.670
Have you made the arrangements
for that bunch of hooligans?

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.540
Yes, sir. We've positioned them
at the first floor entrance.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.420
If we can recapture the hangar bay, we've won.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.000
Chirico, this time, I swear...

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.380
Are they getting ready to start a new push?

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.170
Hey, are we just gonna sit here
and let them kill Chirico?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.960
What would you prefer,
having us three take on the police force?

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.880
That's a ticket to dying early!

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.920
He's right. This once, we can't go.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:43.830
No...

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:52.170
They're trying to flush us out!

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.040
We'll take the elevator down.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.250
Once we're below ground level,
there's a section only I know about.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:01.130
A high-speed subway runs into the service bay.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.880
Did you hear that?

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.960
We're close to the Samarinay subway station.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:08.290
C'mon, let's go!

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.250
I'm against it!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:14.170
We've already risked our lives
enough saving Chirico.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.630
Yeah, it's too dangerous.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.040
I doubt we'd be able to get out alive.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.630
Exactly. We'd better get the hell out of here.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.750
Okay, get going to the subway!

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.960
You...! Quit fooling around.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.460
Coconna, I know how you feel.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.790
But let it go this time.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:35.960
Are you serious?

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.420
I think she's serious.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.420
She is. She is.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:42.330
Come on!

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.380
What do we do, Vanilla?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.290
Not much, with a gun pointed at me.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.380
Guess Coconna wins this one.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.540
All right, let's go!

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.380
All right!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.500
Just let them go!

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:30.250
Run for it!

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.130
Get in the elevator!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.790
It's moving.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.670
It's about time we got into this fight.

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:05.580
Are all the troops dispersed
inside the building perimeter?

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.080
We're weak on the north side.
Better send reinforcements.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:12.750
Roger. Try to coordinate with the Battling team.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:13.960
Battling team?

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:14.960
Chirico!

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.920
If we go up against them,
we could have some trouble.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.500
They're all real battle veterans.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:33.380
Even Chirico can't handle that bunch of killers.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:38.580
It'd be nice if they ended up
killing each other, wouldn't it?

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:40.500
It's from headquarters!

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:42.790
Shut the door.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.380
Why are you having so much trouble
with this one man?!

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:51.290
We've run into some problems
with the Prototype, so...

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.710
No excuses!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:56.170
You were in charge of its conditioning!

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.830
Yes, well...

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:02.580
The one thing you must do
is eliminate Chirico Cuvie!

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:04.790
Yes, sir!

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:05.880
Borough!

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.790
The time has come to abandon Uoodo.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.420
Apparently so.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.830
You'll have to transport the Prototype and
the jijirium out of Uoodo as quickly as possible.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.330
Yes, sir. At once!

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.460
There was a directional bomb in the elevator!

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.710
Where is he?

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:50.500
Above us?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:55.460
No, I don't think he'd want to go toe to toe
with the cops outside.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.500
Underground?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:57.920
That's right! Move it!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.580
All right!

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.830
You can't beat them with an idiotic attack like that.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.710
Chirico, they can track us too easily together.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:33.960
Split up!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.080
Where...

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.380
where are they?

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.420
They may be punks,
but they seem to know how to fight.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:28.000
Sir, Chirico and the Prototype's ATs have been
pursued into the underground service bay.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.130
It's not like Chirico to be caught in plain sight.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.330
Does he have some sort of objective?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:36.960
The police have recruited Battlers to go after him.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.960
Battlers?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.000
The police have put some thought into this.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.670
We have a message from HQ.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.210
Intelligence Officer Rochina, reporting, sir!

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:58.040
I've received word of your situation.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.580
Your conclusions?

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:04.920
Analysis of current data shows
the need for support troops.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:07.130
We have an airborne AT unit en route to you now.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:09.670
They're running about six minutes
behind mission schedule,

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.040
but they should be there soon.

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:14.080
By the way, did you learn
the truth about the police?

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:16.130
Chief Iskui, you mean?

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:20.330
Yes. I assumed he was just a minor player,

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.000
but I learned that after he left
the Gilgamesh Military Academy,

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.040
he was trained as an intelligence operative
in the Melkian special service.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:31.580
After serving as a special agent during the
Balarant operation, he was promoted to major.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.880
I assume the time he was an operative
is what's in question.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.000
I think he was part of the organization

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.920
which attacked the Lido research station
and stole the Prototype.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:42.920
He may be vital in cracking
this secret society open.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:47.330
I'll begin my investigation of him
when the airborne unit arrives.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:50.290
Will you be able to capture him alive?

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:52.500
Leave this to me, sir.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:56.880
From where I stand going up against
these police will be like fighting children.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:04.210
Vanilla, I'm sorry.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.380
Hey, forget it.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.830
Besides, that thing couldn't have fired.

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:13.830
It's a good thing I left the safety on.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:17.630
It keeps it from going off in situations like these.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.420
I thought as much.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.790
Well, let's go.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.460
Now it'll fire.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.420
Hey, what're you doing? C'mon!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.420
Coming!

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.580
Let's hope this thing still works.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:42.960
Hey, it does work!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:21.170
This is 100mm armor!
That thing won't crack it!

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.040
Are you all right?

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.380
Yes, I'm fine.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:48.830
Fyana!

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.170
Are you okay?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.290
Yeah, I think so.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.460
Just before, you called me "Fyana."

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.580
Is that a name you've chosen for me?

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:41.040
It's...

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:43.330
Well, is it?

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:48.170
Save that for later.
We'll have to make a break for it.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:50.040
But which way's the subway?

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.330
Through that wall down there.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.250
I wonder if Chirico's all right.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:24.880
If he died that easily,
we wouldn't be having this much trouble.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.670
Through that wall!

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:48.330
Chirico...

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.380
Here we go!

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:06.540
Chirico, get on!

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.080
I didn't want you caught in this!
Save yourselves!

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:13.330
Oh, you didn't, huh? Well, now we are! Jeez...

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.630
If you don't want us all to die, then get in!

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:16.630
Chirico...

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:17.960
Chirico!

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:25.080
Chirico, get in already!
You wanna get us all killed?!

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:28.420
Would you move it?!

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:33.460
Get us outta here!

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:50.790
What the...?

00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:36.630
Saving you all the time
is getting to be a real pain!

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:42.460
I suppose you're thinking about
that other girl, right?!

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:47.080
Fyana...

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:50.710
But why did I call her that name?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.790
Next Episode

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:58.580
Balls of fire rain down. Armored troopers land.

00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:01.670
Uoodo, city of desires, secrets,
and violence, now burns.

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:05.460
A single-mindedly overwhelming power
now stampedes in.

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:08.960
Whispering desires, budding romance,
bonds, heroic ambitions...

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:13.250
old and young, men and women,
yesterday and tomorrow.

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:15.540
All are swallowed up, running,
in the flames. The flames...

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:17.750
Amidst this tumult, Uoodo is consumed.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:19.540
Next time, "Escape"

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:22.170
The Phoenix is reborn from a fiery destruction.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:24.290
Escape

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
